WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Good to have you on SpaceX Daily, episode 15, coming to you from Vancouver,

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:10.740
it's June 26th, 2026. From the launch pad to the trading floor, here's everything that

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:17.020
moved today. Starpipes dedicated Texas gas line removes a propellant delivery bottle neck that

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:23.660
has caped Starship launch cadence at Starbase. SpaceX plans to build the Starpipes natural gas pipeline

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:29.480
to deliver fuel directly to Starbase for liquid faction into methane and oxygen. Construction

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:37.520
begins in July 2026 with first gas flow expected in 2027. Reports indicate the line is sized to

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:43.200
support multiple Starship flights per week once complete. The project also includes expanded

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:49.720
tank farms and road upgrades at the Texas site. With propellant delivery now moving from truck logistics

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:55.920
to purpose built infrastructure, the next infrastructure push is happening at the Cape. SpaceX has

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.860
already stacked the first two segments of a second mechazilla tower at SLC 37 in Florida.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.720
Observers note the pace matches the 43-day build of the prior tower at Starbase.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:14.160
Completion by late July would give the site a full tower ahead of planned Falcon Heavy and Starship

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.800
operations. The structure is intended to handle both current Falcon Heavy missions and future Starship

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:27.580
flights after pad upgrades. While Texas and Florida infrastructure expands, SpaceX is also

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.140
exploring new ways to deliver connectivity directly from orbit. SpaceX is evaluating a retail

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:40.560
direct to cell service that would use existing Starlink spectrum and satellites rather than new ground

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.200
towers. Initial coverage would target rural areas and highway corridors before any urban expansion.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.120
No formal license application has reached regulators yet, though planning documents outline

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.620
competition with major carriers. As Starlink pushes into new terrestrial markets,

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.180
pressure is building on its existing ride share business. Demand for Falcon 9,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:12.460
transporter, and bandwagon slots now exceed supply for 2026 and 2027. Operators face multi-month

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:18.320
weights and rising per kilogram prices as secondary payloads compete for remaining capacity.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.280
Some small satellite builders are shifting payloads to other vehicles or delaying deployments.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:31.160
SpaceX has not announced additional dedicated small-sat missions to ease the queue. While commercial

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:36.700
ride share capacity tightens, a new weather satellite just proved the value of those same missions.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:44.700
The gems to microwave radiometer on the weather stream satellite launch March 30 on transporter 16

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:51.120
has returned its first global data. The instrument collects cloud penetrating moisture and

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:57.080
temperature profiles across multiple microwave bands. Early validation shows agreement with

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:03.020
radioson measurements within expected error bounds. The mission highlights ongoing commercial

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:09.180
demand for dedicated small-weather satellites on ride share flights. A sunset Falcon 9

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:15.780
ascent from Vandenberg was visible across Southern California on June 25. The booster flew a

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:21.640
standard Starlink mission profile with recovery on the drone ship. No anomalies were reported during

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.960
ascent or landing. Photographers posted time lapses of the Vandenberg sunset plume stretching across

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.840
the Pacific. Observers described the plume as stretching for hundreds of miles under clear evening

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:41.800
conditions. Observers on X noted the rapid initial stacking rate at SLC 37 and compared it directly

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:47.960
to the star-based tower timeline. Small satellite builders discussed shifting some payloads to

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:55.040
non-space-x vehicles after repeated transporter slot delays. Weather data users highlighted the new

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:01.460
GMS-2 microwave channels that fill gaps in tropical moisture tracking. Aviation and maritime

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:06.960
users shared early tests of Starlink direct to cell coverage along remote coastal routes.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:13.600
Worth keeping an eye on, state records reviewed by the Texas Observer show a worker fatality

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.760
at a space-x facility alongside hundreds of reported injuries in recent years.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:24.600
The incident renews questions about safety protocols during high-tempo manufacturing and

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:30.980
launch site construction. Investigations are ongoing and SpaceX has not released a public statement

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:37.560
on corrective actions. On the AI front, no news source developments on orbital data centers or

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:43.960
XAI compute integration appeared in today's coverage. Watchers continue tracking Starlink direct

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:49.560
to cell backhaul capacity and any cross-company compute arrangements that may surface in future

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:55.600
filings. From an engineering standpoint, the Starpipe project centers on moving natural gas from

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:02.820
existing Texas supply points to star-based liquefaction trains. At first principles, the constraint is not

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:08.760
the gas itself, but the rate at which it can be delivered chilled to liquid and stored without venting

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:15.480
losses. A dedicated pipeline collapses the logistics chain that currently relies on truck or rail

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:21.840
deliveries whose throughput is limited by vehicle cycles and road access. Once online, the line

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:27.200
can supply the several hundred tons of methane per flight that a weekly cadence would demand,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:33.660
cutting both cost and schedule risk. The design choice also creates a single point of failure

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:39.660
that must be engineered with redundant compression and leak detection systems to keep launch availability

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:47.520
high. Next milestones to watch are the July groundbreaking and any updates on liquefaction plant capacity

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:52.900
that will determine how many vehicles can be fueled in parallel and a quick market note.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:06:03.780
SBCX closed at $153 up 0.1%. Before we go, watch for any updates on the Starpipe groundbreaking and

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:09.800
whether the SLC-37 tower stacking pace holds through July. And that's a wrap on today's SpaceX

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:19.740
developments. SBCX is trading at $153 up 0.1%. Share this with a fellow spaceflight fan if you found it

